I only pictured it in my head at home.

254
00:08:48,553 --> 00:08:49,893
I had never been here before.

255
00:08:50,063 --> 00:08:51,163
I was confused.

256
00:08:51,493 --> 00:08:53,322
The paths for the head and the back were fairly simple.

257
00:08:53,323 --> 00:08:56,763
But the paths for the fins and the mouth were complicated.

258
00:08:56,863 --> 00:08:59,503
I was the most concerned about those paths.

259
00:08:59,733 --> 00:09:01,533
I didn't know if we had to go right or left.

260
00:09:02,473 --> 00:09:03,643
I was confused then.

261
00:09:04,603 --> 00:09:06,743
- Do we have to go to the store? - Yes.

262
00:09:07,643 --> 00:09:08,643
We have to go this way.

263
00:09:08,644 --> 00:09:09,772
- Which way? - This way.

264
00:09:09,773 --> 00:09:10,842
We have to go this way.

265
00:09:10,843 --> 00:09:12,282
(He kindly helps Hyun Moo find the path.)

266
00:09:12,283 --> 00:09:13,583
Where are we?

267
00:09:13,858 --> 00:09:15,528
- Hyun Moo. - Yes?

268
00:09:15,553 --> 00:09:17,052
- I'm a bit dizzy. - Wait.

269
00:09:17,053 --> 00:09:19,353
- We go down and then turn left. - I'm dizzy.

270
00:09:19,783 --> 00:09:22,523
Then let's buy something at the store.

271
00:09:22,653 --> 00:09:24,462
- How about an iced Americano? - Yes.

272
00:09:24,463 --> 00:09:26,586
Okay. There are chairs too.

273
00:09:26,793 --> 00:09:27,933
Let's go in together.

274
00:09:28,607 --> 00:09:30,402
- Hello. - Hello.

275
00:09:30,403 --> 00:09:31,463
Hello.

276
00:09:31,563 --> 00:09:32,732
Men ought to drink hovenia tea.

277
00:09:32,733 --> 00:09:34,102
- Men ought to drink hovenia tea. - Right.

278
00:09:34,103 --> 00:09:35,632
(They pick their beverages and go to the counter.)

279
00:09:35,633 --> 00:09:36,663
Hello.

280
00:09:36,773 --> 00:09:38,442
- Do you sell lottery tickets? - Yes.

281
00:09:38,443 --> 00:09:40,972
Lottery tickets? Yes. They should all get one.

282
00:09:40,973 --> 00:09:42,913
- I'll buy one for everyone. - Really?

283
00:09:43,243 --> 00:09:45,842
- If anyone wins, we'll split it. - Okay.

284
00:09:45,843 --> 00:09:47,883
- Don't suddenly go off the grid. - Okay.

285
00:09:48,353 --> 00:09:49,983
How much are four lottery tickets?

286
00:09:50,083 --> 00:09:51,453
- I'll pay. - Twenty dollars?

287
00:09:51,983 --> 00:09:53,422
- No. - No, I'll pay.

288
00:09:53,423 --> 00:09:55,253
- Come on. You should rest. - He already wired the money.

289
00:09:55,393 --> 00:09:56,693
- I already did it. - Let's see.

290
00:09:57,093 --> 00:09:58,263
- You did? - Yes.

291
00:09:58,923 --> 00:10:00,493
- He paid for everything. - Grab one.

292
00:10:01,093 --> 00:10:02,262
Thank you.

293
00:10:02,263 --> 00:10:03,463
- Thank you. - Thank you.

294
00:10:05,133 --> 00:10:06,433
- Gosh. - We'll split the winnings.

295
00:10:06,873 --> 00:10:08,072
We're going to split it.

296
00:10:08,073 --> 00:10:09,333
- Guys. Listen. - Let's split it.

297
00:10:09,633 --> 00:10:11,142
Don't suddenly go off the grid or disappear.

298
00:10:11,143 --> 00:10:13,302
- Did you check it? - It was a dud for me.

299
00:10:13,303 --> 00:10:15,813
Oh, I didn't check mine.

300
00:10:15,943 --> 00:10:17,212
- Let's check it now. - Let's check.

301
00:10:17,213 --> 00:10:19,142
- Did you check yours? - I did. I didn't win anything.

302
00:10:19,143 --> 00:10:20,152
You check it.

303
00:10:20,153 --> 00:10:22,113
- I didn't take it out since then. - Let's check it.

304
00:10:22,253 --> 00:10:23,282
Na Ra, don't forget that.

305
00:10:23,283 --> 00:10:25,153
We said we'd split the money if anyone won.

306
00:10:25,883 --> 00:10:27,523
- Gosh. - Seriously?

307
00:10:27,923 --> 00:10:30,222
- None of my numbers matched. - Really?

308
00:10:30,223 --> 00:10:31,922
- "None." - "None?"

309
00:10:31,923 --> 00:10:33,663
- None at all. - Same here.

310
00:10:33,893 --> 00:10:36,133
- Check it with the QR code. - Please.

311
00:10:36,293 --> 00:10:38,033
It'd be crazy if he won 2nd or 3rd place.

312
00:10:38,103 --> 00:10:39,563
- Oh, my! - What is it?

313
00:10:39,903 --> 00:10:41,203
- I won 10 dollars. - He got 10 dollars.

314
00:10:41,903 --> 00:10:43,032
- Let's split it. - He won ten dollars.

315
00:10:43,033 --> 00:10:45,002
- He got 3 numbers? - The ticket costs 5 dollars.

316
00:10:45,003 --> 00:10:46,003
- That's pretty good. - Hey.

317
00:10:46,004 --> 00:10:47,412
I guess things will go well for us.

318
00:10:47,413 --> 00:10:50,283
- Team Moo Do Ra Ji has good luck. - Right. It means we have good luck.

319
00:10:51,213 --> 00:10:53,312
- Give me 2.5 dollars later. - Sure.

320
00:10:53,313 --> 00:10:54,382
- Split it with us too. - Yes.

321
00:10:54,383 --> 00:10:55,482
- Sure. - It's 1.42 dollars.

322
00:10:55,483 --> 00:10:57,052
- It's 1.42 dollars. - So 1.42 dollars for everyone?

323
00:10:57,053 --> 00:10:58,222
- It's 1.428 dollars. - If you want it,

324
00:10:58,223 --> 00:10:59,782
- you must run with us. - Gosh.

325
00:10:59,783 --> 00:11:02,052
- You had my moral support. - My heart is racing.

326
00:11:02,053 --> 00:11:03,963
- We're giving you our support. - Yes.

327
00:11:04,023 --> 00:11:05,093
Right.

328
00:11:05,423 --> 00:11:06,493
What about Dowoon?

329
00:11:07,393 --> 00:11:09,562
- Dowoon. Is that why he's not here? - Why...

330
00:11:09,563 --> 00:11:10,763
- Right. - Is that why he's not here?

331
00:11:11,463 --> 00:11:12,502
That must be it.

332
00:11:12,503 --> 00:11:13,573
Is that why he's not here?

333
00:11:13,733 --> 00:11:14,832
That must be it.

334
00:11:14,833 --> 00:11:16,102
I was wondering why he wasn't here.

335
00:11:16,103 --> 00:11:17,672
(Suspecting Dowoon's whereabouts)

336
00:11:17,673 --> 00:11:19,473
He must've won something. We said we'd split it.

337
00:11:20,713 --> 00:11:22,272
- I'm so full. - You're not tired, right?

338
00:11:22,273 --> 00:11:23,912
(He finally gets to take a much-needed break.)

339
00:11:23,913 --> 00:11:25,413
(Refreshed)

340
00:11:25,743 --> 00:11:27,253
- There's a puppy in the back. - That's such a cute puppy.

341
00:11:29,113 --> 00:11:30,623
- Oh, my. You look so adorable. - So cute.

342
00:11:31,023 --> 00:11:32,323
This is crazy.

343
00:11:33,183 --> 00:11:34,293
That puppy was so cute.

344
00:11:34,723 --> 00:11:35,723
I guess it's a neighborhood dog.

345
00:11:35,724 --> 00:11:37,193
Why do you look so cute?

346
00:11:38,023 --> 00:11:39,093
What?

347
00:11:39,693 --> 00:11:41,363
- I see. - It's food for the dog.

348
00:11:41,693 --> 00:11:43,733
Hyun Moo loves animals.

349
00:11:44,633 --> 00:11:46,732
All right. Here.

350
00:11:46,733 --> 00:11:47,872
- How cute. - So cute.

351
00:11:47,873 --> 00:11:49,703
- Look at this cutie. - That's such a cute puppy.

352
00:11:50,243 --> 00:11:51,973
- What a cute puppy. - You're not hungry?

353
00:11:53,473 --> 00:11:54,712
Does my leg look tastier?

354
00:11:54,713 --> 00:11:56,442
(Showing more interested in his leg than the food)

355
00:11:56,443 --> 00:11:58,042
Hyun Moo, this Fun Run is great.

356
00:11:58,043 --> 00:12:00,612
- You can do whatever you want. - You can.

357
00:12:00,613 --> 00:12:01,712
Seriously. You can do everything.

358
00:12:01,713 --> 00:12:03,113
Time doesn't matter for them.

359
00:12:03,583 --> 00:12:04,683
Give it to me.

360
00:12:05,453 --> 00:12:06,482
Here.

361
00:12:06,483 --> 00:12:08,092
I don't think... Wait, will the puppy eat it?

362
00:12:08,093 --> 00:12:09,122
- No. - Yes.

363
00:12:09,123 --> 00:12:10,563
- Go on. - It had to be around the nose.

364
00:12:10,993 --> 00:12:12,663
Look at you. You're eating it.

365
00:12:13,093 --> 00:12:14,162
Oh, my.

366
00:12:14,163 --> 00:12:16,563
That was the happiest and most therapeutic moment.

367
00:12:17,563 --> 00:12:18,703
Is it good?

368
00:12:20,233 --> 00:12:21,832
So we just have to complete the belly part?

369
00:12:21,833 --> 00:12:23,772
Listen. We completed the tail,

370
00:12:23,773 --> 00:12:25,372
the back, the head,

371
00:12:25,373 --> 00:12:26,642
and the fin too.

372
00:12:26,643 --> 00:12:28,873
- The belly is the only thing left. - The belly.

373
00:12:29,343 --> 00:12:30,412
- We're almost done then. - The belly part.

374
00:12:30,413 --> 00:12:31,643
- It's almost over. - Yes.

375
00:12:32,143 --> 00:12:33,512
- It gets harder when we rest. - Let's get going.

376
00:12:33,513 --> 00:12:34,582
Let's start running.

377
00:12:34,583 --> 00:12:36,112
- It was great, sir. - Sure.

378
00:12:36,113 --> 00:12:37,253
- Thank you. - Okay.

379
00:12:37,723 --> 00:12:38,882
- Chief Moo. - Yes.

380
00:12:38,883 --> 00:12:39,953
- Let's get going. - Let's start running.

381
00:12:40,123 --> 00:12:41,723
- Okay. - It's colder when we don't run.

382
00:12:42,123 --> 00:12:43,662
- If you rest too long, - We have to keep running.

383
00:12:43,663 --> 00:12:45,193
- your body will get stiff. - From the end...

384
00:12:45,863 --> 00:12:48,633
We have to decide whether we'll turn left or right.

385
00:12:49,293 --> 00:12:51,703
If we turn left, we'll complete the belly.

386
00:12:52,603 --> 00:12:54,233
- Okay. - If we turn right,

387
00:12:54,333 --> 00:12:55,573
we can also trace the mouth line.

388
00:12:55,803 --> 00:12:57,503
Will it be a mouthless whale...

389
00:12:57,803 --> 00:12:59,103
or a whale with a mouth?

390
00:12:59,573 --> 00:13:01,473
To do that, we have to go back and forth, right?

391
00:13:02,143 --> 00:13:03,213
That will be the mouth.

392
00:13:03,343 --> 00:13:04,412
Then let's turn there.

393
00:13:04,413 --> 00:13:05,643
(Fully motivated)

394
00:13:06,843 --> 00:13:08,582
(They choose to turn right to give the whale a mouth.)

395
00:13:08,583 --> 00:13:09,652
- Hello. - Let's go.

396
00:13:09,653 --> 00:13:11,283
(They choose to turn right to give the whale a mouth.)

397
00:13:11,853 --> 00:13:13,582
You know what? I love it.

398
00:13:13,583 --> 00:13:15,223
Yes. Look at the view.

399
00:13:16,653 --> 00:13:20,833
(Running while admiring the ocean view)

400
00:13:21,263 --> 00:13:23,032
Hey, our crew song isn't getting us...

401
00:13:23,033 --> 00:13:24,803
- pumped up at all. - Right.

402
00:13:24,933 --> 00:13:27,403
Ji Hyeon, do you know any song that can get our energy up?

403
00:13:28,033 --> 00:13:29,473
Let's see.

404
00:13:30,473 --> 00:13:31,902
- How about this song, Dowoon? - What?

405
00:13:31,903 --> 00:13:33,973
I ran

406
00:13:34,273 --> 00:13:36,112
I ran

407
00:13:36,113 --> 00:13:37,482
(Smirking)

408
00:13:37,483 --> 00:13:38,543
That's great.

409
00:13:40,143 --> 00:13:42,483
- I ran - I ran

410
00:13:42,883 --> 00:13:45,082
- For you - I can't watch this.

411
00:13:45,083 --> 00:13:47,592
(The crew chief is excited with the songwriter's permission.)

412
00:13:47,593 --> 00:13:51,163
- Moo Do Ra Ji for you - For you

413
00:13:51,623 --> 00:13:53,092
For you

414
00:13:53,093 --> 00:13:55,193
(We can't leave out our crew name in the team anthem.)

415
00:13:55,693 --> 00:13:58,333
- Moo Do Ra Ji - Moo Do Ra Ji

416
00:13:58,663 --> 00:14:00,302
- My gosh. - Isn't that nice?

417
00:14:00,303 --> 00:14:02,333
I can't keep watching this.

418
00:14:03,703 --> 00:14:08,313
(Their 2nd team anthem pushes them to complete the mouth.)

419
00:14:09,143 --> 00:14:10,883
(While enjoying the run...)

420
00:14:12,013 --> 00:14:13,413
Gosh, that place looks nice.

421
00:14:13,543 --> 00:14:16,613
- How beautiful. - Dowoon. This ocean is crazy

422
00:14:19,023 --> 00:14:20,923
I told you I hated this kind of thing the most.

423
00:14:22,623 --> 00:14:25,192
(But just like he said, there's a crazy view of the ocean.)

424
00:14:25,193 --> 00:14:27,492
- It's so beautiful. - I can't believe this.

425
00:14:27,493 --> 00:14:29,532
Is that the observatory you saw from the ground earlier?

426
00:14:29,533 --> 00:14:31,302
Right. That's the same spot.

427
00:14:31,303 --> 00:14:32,533
(Observatory)

428
00:14:32,763 --> 00:14:35,473
- Gosh, this is insane. - This is crazy.

429
00:14:36,503 --> 00:14:38,202
- This is crazy. - It's incredible.

430
00:14:38,203 --> 00:14:39,442
- It's the charm of the East Sea. - Gosh.

431
00:14:39,443 --> 00:14:41,772
The panoramic view was nothing but the ocean.

432
00:14:41,773 --> 00:14:42,942
- Right. - It was really nice.

433
00:14:42,943 --> 00:14:44,643
I had never seen such a vast ocean like this.

434
00:14:45,583 --> 00:14:46,982
- This is incredible. - Gosh.

435
00:14:46,983 --> 00:14:49,083
- The view here is insane. - It's so beautiful here.

436
00:14:50,283 --> 00:14:51,582
Let's walk around.

437
00:14:51,583 --> 00:14:53,083
- Yes. Sounds good. - We should do that.

438
00:14:54,453 --> 00:14:56,222
(They stop running and will have fun now.)

439
00:14:56,223 --> 00:14:57,892
- That's how the port looked before. - I like the vibe here.

440
00:14:57,893 --> 00:14:58,963
- Gosh. - This is nice indeed.

441
00:14:59,193 --> 00:15:01,162
Hey, it's crazy. They set this place up really well.

442
00:15:01,163 --> 00:15:02,733
No wonder why a lot of zoomers come here.

443
00:15:02,893 --> 00:15:04,433
- Yes. - I see.

444
00:15:06,063 --> 00:15:08,032
(Let me see.)

445
00:15:08,033 --> 00:15:09,233
(What's that?)

446
00:15:11,103 --> 00:15:12,272
- What's this now? - Hello.

447
00:15:12,273 --> 00:15:13,912
- Hello. - Hello.

448
00:15:13,913 --> 00:15:15,742
- Hello. - Four adults.

449
00:15:15,743 --> 00:15:17,482
- Four adults? - Yes.

450
00:15:17,483 --> 00:15:20,113
We have a few activities you can try. Will you try them too?

451
00:15:20,483 --> 00:15:22,912
We have the Sky Cycle and the Giant Slide.

452
00:15:22,913 --> 00:15:24,282
- Gosh. - You can take them to go down?

453
00:15:24,283 --> 00:15:25,982
- Hey, these look fun. - I didn't know about them either.

454
00:15:25,983 --> 00:15:27,853
- Oh, my. - "Sky Cycle?"

455
00:15:28,193 --> 00:15:29,523
I can't do it. It's too scary.

456
00:15:30,023 --> 00:15:31,393
- He was scared of these activities. - I'm scared.

457
00:15:31,793 --> 00:15:33,092
Hold on. I'll talk to my team.

458
00:15:33,093 --> 00:15:34,162
- What's this? - What did you say?

459
00:15:34,163 --> 00:15:35,232
- This looks scary. - No, it doesn't.

460
00:15:35,233 --> 00:15:36,933
We can get on these rides.

461
00:15:37,703 --> 00:15:39,062
There's safety gear.

462
00:15:39,063 --> 00:15:41,372
(A bicycle is suspended 21m high in the sky.)

463
00:15:41,373 --> 00:15:43,103
- You're scared of this? - Yes.

464
00:15:43,233 --> 00:15:44,743
- Why? - I'm scared of it.

465
00:15:45,343 --> 00:15:48,372
The Giant Slide doesn't look dangerous.

466
00:15:48,373 --> 00:15:50,212
- That one's fine. - You think this might be dangerous?

467
00:15:50,213 --> 00:15:51,982
- Yes. - In case the ropes snap?

468
00:15:51,983 --> 00:15:53,782
- Yes. - Has that ever happened before?

469
00:15:53,783 --> 00:15:54,882
No.

470
00:15:54,883 --> 00:15:58,583
(No!)

471
00:15:58,683 --> 00:16:00,652
- "No!" - She got mad at us.

472
00:16:00,653 --> 00:16:01,692
(Flustered)

473
00:16:01,693 --> 00:16:03,352
Just try it. I'm sure we'll be fine.

474
00:16:03,353 --> 00:16:04,623
Everything is tightly secured.

475
00:16:05,063 --> 00:16:06,722
It's all right. All of us will try it.

476
00:16:06,723 --> 00:16:07,732
- Okay. - Let's go.

477
00:16:07,733 --> 00:16:09,132
- I'll charge you for four people. - Four people.

478
00:16:09,133 --> 00:16:11,503
- Let's try the activities here. - Let's go.

479
00:16:13,233 --> 00:16:18,243
(They set out to try the activity.)

480
00:16:19,073 --> 00:16:21,173
I didn't expect us to end up at a fun place like that.

481
00:16:21,373 --> 00:16:23,612
I didn't plan anything down to the details.

482
00:16:23,613 --> 00:16:25,812
All of a sudden, we stumbled across this amazing place.

483
00:16:25,813 --> 00:16:27,253
And that's the perk of the Fun Run.

484
00:16:27,753 --> 00:16:29,582
Stressed runners always...

485
00:16:29,583 --> 00:16:32,383
go on the same predetermined routes like machines.

486
00:16:32,583 --> 00:16:34,222
They would never get to experience this thrill.

487
00:16:34,223 --> 00:16:35,693
Stressed runners?

488
00:16:35,823 --> 00:16:37,263
What are you talking about?

489
00:16:37,593 --> 00:16:38,962
Here's what I noticed...

490
00:16:38,963 --> 00:16:40,293
- about your crew. - Right.

491
00:16:40,533 --> 00:16:42,963
Everyone looks happy, and it looks like a fun run.

492
00:16:43,233 --> 00:16:45,732
But you have an inferiority complex against serious runners.

493
00:16:45,733 --> 00:16:47,202
- Yes, he does. - His inferiority complex...

494
00:16:47,203 --> 00:16:48,572
- is on another level. - He keeps on provoking us.

495
00:16:48,573 --> 00:16:50,502
- I mean... - Why do you keep provoking me?

496
00:16:50,503 --> 00:16:52,642
- Seriously. - We're happy too when we run.

497
00:16:52,643 --> 00:16:54,142
He really went for it.

498
00:16:54,143 --> 00:16:55,343
No. I didn't.

499
00:16:57,513 --> 00:16:58,683
This is it.

500
00:16:59,613 --> 00:17:00,953
- That's the Sky Cycle. - What?

501
00:17:01,113 --> 00:17:02,712
- We can go down after that. - For real?

502
00:17:02,713 --> 00:17:05,082
- I see. - Wait. How can I get on that thing?

503
00:17:05,083 --> 00:17:06,323
- Let me see. - This is it.

504
00:17:06,723 --> 00:17:09,193
You ride the bicycle on a rope.

505
00:17:09,753 --> 00:17:11,092
There's no net underneath?

506
00:17:11,093 --> 00:17:12,492
- There's no net? - No.

507
00:17:12,493 --> 00:17:14,192
- Then... - Oh, no.

508
00:17:14,193 --> 00:17:15,462
- That looks scary! - How can you ride that?

509
00:17:15,463 --> 00:17:16,692
It looks scary.

510
00:17:16,693 --> 00:17:18,463
- That's... - I can't ride that. Oh, no.

511
00:17:18,633 --> 00:17:19,802
Actually, I didn't want to do it either.

512
00:17:19,803 --> 00:17:22,332
I was just as scared of heights as Ji Hyeon.

513
00:17:22,333 --> 00:17:23,673
- I see. - You were?

514
00:17:24,373 --> 00:17:26,102
Hello. Is this a round trip?

515
00:17:26,103 --> 00:17:27,242
- Pardon? - Is this a round trip?

516
00:17:27,243 --> 00:17:28,912
- It's a round trip. - I see.

517
00:17:28,913 --> 00:17:30,113
- Oh, that's even worse. - Yes.

518
00:17:30,513 --> 00:17:32,812
Then why don't we try this, Hyun Moo?

519
00:17:32,813 --> 00:17:35,012
- We're real men. - We'll go first.

520
00:17:35,013 --> 00:17:36,312
Wait here and watch.

521
00:17:36,313 --> 00:17:38,383
- Okay. - The youngest is full of energy.

522
00:17:38,423 --> 00:17:39,752
He stepped up.

523
00:17:39,753 --> 00:17:41,893
- So he's not scared of heights. - He's not.

524
00:17:42,623 --> 00:17:44,563
- There's a locker. - A locker?

525
00:17:44,823 --> 00:17:46,392
- There's been an accident? - Anything that could fall out...

526
00:17:46,393 --> 00:17:47,792
(Shocked)

527
00:17:47,793 --> 00:17:49,792
See? People mishear things when they're scared.

528
00:17:49,793 --> 00:17:51,303
- Everything... - Right.

529
00:17:51,903 --> 00:17:53,033
Can you look down, though?

530
00:17:53,663 --> 00:17:54,733
Of course.

531
00:17:55,333 --> 00:17:58,043
(That's impressive.)

532
00:17:58,373 --> 00:17:59,803
- I'll turn around. - Okay.

533
00:18:00,503 --> 00:18:01,643
I can guarantee this.

534
00:18:02,143 --> 00:18:03,172
I can ride anything except for those vertical drops.

535
00:18:03,173 --> 00:18:04,183
Really?

536
00:18:04,543 --> 00:18:06,183
I just don't want to be dropped.

537
00:18:06,843 --> 00:18:08,313
As long as it's horizontal,

538
00:18:08,883 --> 00:18:10,923
I can even go out of the atmosphere.

539
00:18:11,923 --> 00:18:13,453
This isn't scary at all.

540
00:18:14,823 --> 00:18:16,352
(Peaceful)

541
00:18:16,353 --> 00:18:17,393
Okay.

542
00:18:17,893 --> 00:18:19,723
- You got this, Dowoon. - You got this, Dowoon.

543
00:18:21,033 --> 00:18:23,092
Na Ra, there's nothing underneath.

544
00:18:23,093 --> 00:18:24,462
Exactly. Goodbye.

545
00:18:24,463 --> 00:18:26,402
- Okay. - "Goodbye."

546
00:18:26,403 --> 00:18:27,573
What a nice friend you are.

547
00:18:28,033 --> 00:18:29,233
"Goodbye."

548
00:18:29,473 --> 00:18:31,203
There's nothing under this.

549
00:18:31,643 --> 00:18:33,802
That must be scary for people who are afraid of heights.

550
00:18:33,803 --> 00:18:35,213
- Of course. - Let's go.

551
00:18:35,273 --> 00:18:37,043
Look at the flowers on your way there.

552
00:18:37,113 --> 00:18:38,983
Then look at the ocean on your way back.

553
00:18:39,813 --> 00:18:41,752
(All the preparation is done.)

554
00:18:41,753 --> 00:18:43,153
Going back and forth...

555
00:18:43,713 --> 00:18:45,252
Okay. Let's go, Moo Do Ra Ji.

556
00:18:45,253 --> 00:18:47,323
- Let's go, Moo Do Ra Ji. - Let's go.

557
00:18:48,023 --> 00:18:49,993
- Start pedaling now. - I can just go?

558
00:18:50,553 --> 00:18:51,622
- What? - Go slowly.

559
00:18:51,623 --> 00:18:52,722
- He wasn't scared at all. - Go slowly.

560
00:18:52,723 --> 00:18:54,462
- He's going? - He doesn't get scared.

561
00:18:54,463 --> 00:18:55,562
Start pedaling slowly.

562
00:18:55,563 --> 00:18:57,193
- Good luck. - Go slowly.

563
00:18:58,103 --> 00:18:59,932
- Good luck. - Hey, Dowoon!

564
00:18:59,933 --> 00:19:01,333
(Hyun Moo and Dowoon set out slowly.)

565
00:19:02,273 --> 00:19:03,432
(A dizzying height)

566
00:19:03,433 --> 00:19:04,602
It's pretty high.

567
00:19:04,603 --> 00:19:05,942
- It's high. - This is crazy.

568
00:19:05,943 --> 00:19:07,172
Hey, Dowoon!

569
00:19:07,173 --> 00:19:09,572
(Chuckling)

570
00:19:09,573 --> 00:19:10,713
This is crazy.

571
00:19:11,813 --> 00:19:12,943
This is super scary.

572
00:19:12,983 --> 00:19:14,252
- Super scary. - I can even go out...

573
00:19:14,253 --> 00:19:15,482
of the atmosphere.

574
00:19:15,483 --> 00:19:17,653
- Hey! - How can anyone do that?

575
00:19:17,983 --> 00:19:19,123
Dowoon!

576
00:19:19,353 --> 00:19:21,422
You said you could easily handle any horizontal rides.

577
00:19:21,423 --> 00:19:22,653
I realized I couldn't once I was out there.

578
00:19:22,693 --> 00:19:24,193
Gosh, I hate it.

579
00:19:24,363 --> 00:19:25,622
Look at Dowoon pedaling forward.

580
00:19:25,623 --> 00:19:27,193
(Dowoon quickly goes ahead.)

581
00:19:28,193 --> 00:19:31,663
(Giggling)

582
00:19:33,333 --> 00:19:34,333
How can anyone do that?

583
00:19:34,334 --> 00:19:35,373
(Just watching them gives him goosebumps.)

584
00:19:35,633 --> 00:19:36,772
Look at Dowoon go.

585
00:19:36,773 --> 00:19:38,503
- He's just pushing through. - Dowoon makes it look so easy.

586
00:19:40,003 --> 00:19:41,342
Gosh, this is so scary.

587
00:19:41,343 --> 00:19:42,412
Dowoon is killing it.

588
00:19:42,413 --> 00:19:43,872
That's such a cute smile.

589
00:19:43,873 --> 00:19:44,912
- He's happy... - It's not stopping.

590
00:19:44,913 --> 00:19:45,983
as long as we're not running.

591
00:19:47,513 --> 00:19:49,483
What? Wait.

592
00:19:49,883 --> 00:19:51,152
Chief Moo froze.

593
00:19:51,153 --> 00:19:53,683
(He prefers having fun to running.)

594
00:19:53,983 --> 00:19:55,223
Hey. This is super scary.

595
00:19:56,023 --> 00:19:57,053
Dowoon!

596
00:19:57,823 --> 00:19:59,722
- And that's a long ride. - It is.

597
00:19:59,723 --> 00:20:01,562
- It's longer than I expected. - How can I do this? This is crazy.

598
00:20:01,563 --> 00:20:02,632
I couldn't look down.

599
00:20:02,633 --> 00:20:03,992
- I'm not doing this again. - Look at that.

600
00:20:03,993 --> 00:20:05,203
- Oh, my. - Gosh.

601
00:20:05,263 --> 00:20:06,903
- Look at this. I'm up in the air. - Dowoon.

602
00:20:07,403 --> 00:20:09,302
- There was nothing underneath. - This is crazy. Gosh.

603
00:20:09,303 --> 00:20:10,902
My goodness. It's shaking.

604
00:20:10,903 --> 00:20:12,542
(The two runners are flying over the whale's mouth.)

605
00:20:12,543 --> 00:20:13,602
This is so scary.

606
00:20:13,603 --> 00:20:15,613
(Hyun Moo makes a fuss when Dowoon looks at ease.)

607
00:20:16,443 --> 00:20:17,543
I'm here.

608
00:20:19,513 --> 00:20:21,913
(He passes the turning point as if it's nothing.)

609
00:20:22,653 --> 00:20:23,783
Oh, my.

610
00:20:24,483 --> 00:20:25,553
My goodness.

611
00:20:26,623 --> 00:20:29,653
Goodness. It won't move forward. What do I do then?

612
00:20:29,823 --> 00:20:31,562
- Goodness. It won't move forward. - Why not?

613
00:20:31,563 --> 00:20:33,062
- It was not because of your legs? - I see.

614
00:20:33,063 --> 00:20:36,032
The closer you get to the middle, the looser the rope gets.

615
00:20:36,033 --> 00:20:37,402
Right. It has to go up.

616
00:20:37,403 --> 00:20:38,433
Oh, no.

617
00:20:39,333 --> 00:20:41,233
Dowoon, if this doesn't move forward, I'll have to stay still.

618
00:20:41,733 --> 00:20:42,803
What?

619
00:20:43,073 --> 00:20:44,942
- You must get here first. Hurry. - It's not that.

620
00:20:44,943 --> 00:20:46,303
What were you trying to say?

621
00:20:47,643 --> 00:20:50,142
- I'll go first. - Come on. Wait for me.

622
00:20:50,143 --> 00:20:51,613
My gosh. This is so scary.

623
00:20:51,813 --> 00:20:52,982
How can I...

624
00:20:52,983 --> 00:20:54,042
(Glancing down)

625
00:20:54,043 --> 00:20:55,182
I almost peed my pants.

626
00:20:55,183 --> 00:20:58,152
(Scared)

627
00:20:58,153 --> 00:20:59,822
- Right. You almost did. - Hear me out.

628
00:20:59,823 --> 00:21:01,853
I stopped for a second in the middle.

629
00:21:02,253 --> 00:21:03,892
If you don't pedal, you'll just get stuck in the middle.

630
00:21:03,893 --> 00:21:05,422
- Right. - My gosh.

631
00:21:05,423 --> 00:21:06,493
That's so scary.

632
00:21:06,663 --> 00:21:08,993
This is scary. I don't think Ji Hyeon can do this.

633
00:21:10,263 --> 00:21:11,963
(Staring)

634
00:21:12,833 --> 00:21:14,232
My gosh, this is so scary.

635
00:21:14,233 --> 00:21:15,933
(Getting the chills)

636
00:21:16,303 --> 00:21:17,443
Here I go.

637
00:21:19,403 --> 00:21:21,473
(He sets out after Dowoon as he shakes in fear.)

638
00:21:22,743 --> 00:21:24,442
(Pedaling furiously fast)

639
00:21:24,443 --> 00:21:25,742
- Dowoon got the hang of it. - Dowoon, stop.

640
00:21:25,743 --> 00:21:28,112
- That's fast. - I'm up high.

641
00:21:28,113 --> 00:21:30,753
(Fully enjoying the adrenaline rush)

642
00:21:31,553 --> 00:21:33,922
- Oh, my. Okay. - Come all the way in.

643
00:21:33,923 --> 00:21:36,793
(Finishing the ride in a fun mood)

644
00:21:37,023 --> 00:21:38,062
My gosh.

645
00:21:38,063 --> 00:21:40,663
(He moves along while enjoying the view.)

646
00:21:41,233 --> 00:21:42,533
Wave for us.

647
00:21:45,303 --> 00:21:46,803
(Lifting his hand)

648
00:21:47,163 --> 00:21:48,232
Just for a second.

649
00:21:48,233 --> 00:21:49,332
(Lifting his hands)

650
00:21:49,333 --> 00:21:50,973
- I couldn't do it. - You're playful.

651
00:21:53,373 --> 00:21:54,373
(Moomoo returns safely too.)

652
00:21:54,374 --> 00:21:55,572
Hey, you were so good at this.

653
00:21:55,573 --> 00:21:56,673
Did you look down?

654
00:21:56,873 --> 00:21:58,443
- You'd pee your pants then. - It's scary.

655
00:21:59,743 --> 00:22:01,113
Try it. It's fun.

656
00:22:01,553 --> 00:22:03,752
You just said it was scary.

657
00:22:03,753 --> 00:22:06,222
It's scary on your way there, but it's so fun on your way back.

658
00:22:06,223 --> 00:22:07,322
(The crew chief wants everyone to try this fun activity.)

659
00:22:07,323 --> 00:22:08,353
Try it.

660
00:22:08,523 --> 00:22:09,592
Let's try it.

661
00:22:09,593 --> 00:22:11,222
- You'd be curious, though. - Let me explain.

662
00:22:11,223 --> 00:22:13,292
- Right. - It won't catch you off guard.

663
00:22:13,293 --> 00:22:14,793
- Right. - Try it.

664
00:22:15,363 --> 00:22:16,892
- Ji Hyeon. - Let's just get it over with.

665
00:22:16,893 --> 00:22:18,233
- Okay. - Let's do it.

666
00:22:18,403 --> 00:22:19,403
Just get it over with.

667
00:22:19,404 --> 00:22:20,562
- He'll try it? - Na Ra.

668
00:22:20,563 --> 00:22:21,572
This will be so scary for him.

669
00:22:21,573 --> 00:22:24,242
I thought this was my only chance to try something like this.

670
00:22:24,243 --> 00:22:25,672
- That's so cool. - So I gave it a try.

671
00:22:25,673 --> 00:22:26,973
- He didn't show his fear. - Seriously.

672
00:22:27,003 --> 00:22:28,812
- Right. - If you had not done it,

673
00:22:28,813 --> 00:22:29,973
this would've haunted you forever.

674
00:22:30,473 --> 00:22:31,882
So if I had not done it,

675
00:22:31,883 --> 00:22:33,842
you would've made fun of me forever.

676
00:22:33,843 --> 00:22:34,952
I would've mentioned it...

677
00:22:34,953 --> 00:22:36,053
- for over half a year. - Right.

678
00:22:36,183 --> 00:22:37,522
- So you didn't want him to do that. - You would've mocked me...

679
00:22:37,523 --> 00:22:38,652
- and called me a chicken. - You didn't want him to do that.

680
00:22:38,653 --> 00:22:40,422
I knew he would mention that every time he saw me.

681
00:22:40,423 --> 00:22:41,593
(He knew that Hyun Moo would call him a chicken.)

682
00:22:42,723 --> 00:22:45,063
What's this? It keeps getting stuck. Okay.

683
00:22:45,223 --> 00:22:47,023
- Just keep on pedaling. - Okay.

684
00:22:48,093 --> 00:22:49,393
He's nervous.

685
00:22:49,493 --> 00:22:50,533
Of course, it's scary.

686
00:22:51,863 --> 00:22:53,402
I'm really sorry.

687
00:22:53,403 --> 00:22:56,403
But could you check my gear one last time?

688
00:22:59,073 --> 00:23:01,612
- He must double check it. - Why are you such a chicken?

689
00:23:01,613 --> 00:23:03,412
- How could he not? - I was so scared.

690
00:23:03,413 --> 00:23:04,642
- Ji Hyeon... - Just in case.

691
00:23:04,643 --> 00:23:06,712
- Of course. - He's so cute.

692
00:23:06,713 --> 00:23:08,683
My motto is safety first.

693
00:23:09,153 --> 00:23:10,812
- That's really important. - You know,

694
00:23:10,813 --> 00:23:12,953
- when I get on rollercoasters, - Yes.

695
00:23:13,123 --> 00:23:14,593
I check the bar 300 times.

696
00:23:15,353 --> 00:23:17,193
Hey, you might break it then.

697
00:23:17,523 --> 00:23:19,192
- Everyone feels the same way. - Right.

698
00:23:19,193 --> 00:23:20,563
- Yes. - You must double check it.

699
00:23:21,333 --> 00:23:22,792
Why do you want to double check it?

700
00:23:22,793 --> 00:23:25,263
Could you check my harness one more time?

701
00:23:25,363 --> 00:23:27,263
- The harness looks perfect. - Please.

702
00:23:27,463 --> 00:23:29,202
- Thank you. - Just don't cry, Ji Hyeon.

703
00:23:29,203 --> 00:23:30,672
- You got this. - You got this, Ji Hyeon.

704
00:23:30,673 --> 00:23:31,942
You can do this. Let's go.

705
00:23:31,943 --> 00:23:33,403
- Let's go! - Go!

706
00:23:33,573 --> 00:23:34,812
- Let's go. - Go.

707
00:23:34,813 --> 00:23:36,712
- My gosh. - Why am I nervous for him?

708
00:23:36,713 --> 00:23:37,842
- He must pedal hard. - Hold on.

709
00:23:37,843 --> 00:23:40,213
- The first step must be tough. - Keep pedaling.

710
00:23:41,613 --> 00:23:43,912
Oh, my. This is crazy.

711
00:23:43,913 --> 00:23:45,153
(They slowly move forward.)

712
00:23:47,023 --> 00:23:48,222
Both of them are handling it well.

713
00:23:48,223 --> 00:23:49,292
(The two scaredy-cats move forward smoothly.)

714
00:23:49,293 --> 00:23:50,553
They look great.

715
00:23:51,423 --> 00:23:52,623
They're not so scared.

716
00:23:53,263 --> 00:23:54,792
This is driving me crazy.

717
00:23:54,793 --> 00:23:58,363
(This is driving me crazy.)

718
00:23:59,563 --> 00:24:02,402
- Ji Hyeon. - This is driving me crazy. Come on.

719
00:24:02,403 --> 00:24:04,373
(The scared brothers whine shortly after departing.)

720
00:24:07,073 --> 00:24:08,413
- It's so windy! - Oh, the wind!

721
00:24:09,873 --> 00:24:10,873
(A sudden gust of wind hits them.)

722
00:24:10,874 --> 00:24:12,942
- Why is it so windy? - Do you see my shirt fluttering?

723
00:24:12,943 --> 00:24:14,382
- It was very windy that day. - I can see that.

724
00:24:14,383 --> 00:24:15,753
- Your shirt is fluttering. - Let's go.

725
00:24:16,153 --> 00:24:18,422
- Okay, Ji Hyeon. Let's go together. - Please.

726
00:24:18,423 --> 00:24:21,022
- Yes, please. - Let's go at the same pace.

727
00:24:21,023 --> 00:24:22,623
This is indeed safe, right?

728
00:24:23,693 --> 00:24:25,122
Why did they make such a thing?

729
00:24:25,123 --> 00:24:26,722
(Why did they make such a thing?)

730
00:24:26,723 --> 00:24:27,932
Why did they make such a thing?

731
00:24:27,933 --> 00:24:29,893
(I totally agree.)

732
00:24:31,163 --> 00:24:33,733
(With a fundamental question,)

733
00:24:33,863 --> 00:24:36,532
(he reaches the halfway point.)

734
00:24:36,533 --> 00:24:37,842
Gosh, I'm tearing up.

735
00:24:37,843 --> 00:24:39,642
(Gosh, I'm tearing up.)

736
00:24:39,643 --> 00:24:40,703
I'm tearing up.

737
00:24:41,473 --> 00:24:43,912
(Na Ra, same here.)

738
00:24:43,913 --> 00:24:45,243
It's so scary.

739
00:24:46,743 --> 00:24:47,813
It's so scary.

740
00:24:48,383 --> 00:24:49,612
When you're up there,

741
00:24:49,613 --> 00:24:50,853
- you can't look down. - That's right.

742
00:24:51,253 --> 00:24:52,652
It feels so strange. You can't even see the wire.

743
00:24:52,653 --> 00:24:54,652
- I know. - It's scary.

744
00:24:54,653 --> 00:24:56,422
- Ji Hyeon, the wind is the kick. - I know.

745
00:24:56,423 --> 00:24:58,193
- Let's go at the same pace. - Okay.

746
00:24:58,623 --> 00:25:00,323
- You go together when it's scary. - That's right.

747
00:25:02,693 --> 00:25:03,763
My goodness.

748
00:25:03,963 --> 00:25:07,703
(He gets back on the bicycle again as he lets out a big sigh.)

749
00:25:08,103 --> 00:25:09,702
- Ji Hyeon, shall we go? - Okay. Let's go.

750
00:25:09,703 --> 00:25:11,473
Let's go. Ji Hyeon, let's do this.

751
00:25:12,003 --> 00:25:13,772
- Moo Do Ra Ji, let's go! - Moo Do Ra Ji, let's go.

752
00:25:13,773 --> 00:25:14,773
Let's go.

753
00:25:16,573 --> 00:25:17,942
Ma'am, I'm really sorry,

754
00:25:17,943 --> 00:25:19,882
but would you check my safety gear once more?

755
00:25:19,883 --> 00:25:21,853
Hey, you punk!

756
00:25:22,453 --> 00:25:24,623
- Ma'am, I'm really sorry... - Hold on.

757
00:25:24,753 --> 00:25:27,323
- His safety gear! - They were supposed to go together!

758
00:25:27,553 --> 00:25:28,692
Then he went, "Hold on."

759
00:25:28,693 --> 00:25:30,692
- What was that? - I had to be certain.

760
00:25:30,693 --> 00:25:31,992
- Ji Hyeon. - You always go, "I'm sorry, but..."

761
00:25:31,993 --> 00:25:32,993
Ji Hyeon.

762
00:25:32,994 --> 00:25:34,062
I had to be certain.

763
00:25:34,063 --> 00:25:36,593
Na Ra, that was your reaction. I seriously had no idea.

764
00:25:36,833 --> 00:25:39,862
You should've asked her to check Na Ra's safety gear as well.

765
00:25:39,863 --> 00:25:41,172
- I know. - Na Ra was off,

766
00:25:41,173 --> 00:25:42,632
but you asked the staff to check your safety gear.

767
00:25:42,633 --> 00:25:44,133
- "Please check my safety gear." - Why did you do that?

768
00:25:44,303 --> 00:25:45,472
It was the first day we met.

769
00:25:45,473 --> 00:25:47,342
- And Ji Hyeon disappointed me. - Na Ra was off.

770
00:25:47,343 --> 00:25:48,613
- He disappointed you. - That's right.

771
00:25:49,373 --> 00:25:50,872
- I mean, Na Ra... - You went, "Hey, you punk!"

772
00:25:50,873 --> 00:25:52,382
I can tell that you guys are close.

773
00:25:52,383 --> 00:25:54,242
To be honest, I didn't even think about Na Ra.

774
00:25:54,243 --> 00:25:55,652
That's right.

775
00:25:55,653 --> 00:25:57,012
